      "source": "prose",
      "promptMarkdown": "Audit the accessibility of the sign-up page below. You have its source only; you cannot open it in a browser.\n\n~~~html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>Sign up</title>\n  <style>\n    body { font-family: sans-serif; color: #222; background: #fff; }\n    .btn { display: inline-block; padding: 4px 8px; background: #0a58ca; color: #fff; }\n    :focus { outline: none; }\n    .hint { color: #595959; font-size: 0.9rem; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <img src=\"/img/logo-2024-final.png\">\n  <h1>Create your account</h1>\n  <form id=\"signup\">\n    <input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" id=\"email\">\n    <input type=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\" id=\"email\">\n    <p class=\"hint\">At least 8 characters.</p>\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"terms\"> I accept the terms</label>\n    <a href=\"/terms\" tabindex=\"3\">Read the terms</a>\n    <div class=\"btn\" onclick=\"submitForm()\">Create account</div>\n  </form>\n  <script>\n    function submitForm() { document.getElementById(\"signup\").submit(); }\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n~~~\n\nWhere information is missing, state your assumption and continue; do not ask questions. Reply with the deliverable only, as Markdown, starting at its first line, with no introduction and no code fence around it. Do not create or edit files.",
